{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775326859-tlp5NL0X9dzBpzCp38K8","role":"assistant","created":1775326880,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the data, I need to understand what's being asked:\n\n1. The question asks about the \"Employment and General Retirement net budget receipts\" \n2. It wants the percent growth from the month that FY2013 budget proposal was released to the month that FY2023 budget proposal was supposed to be released\n3. The data is in nominal dollars\n\nI see two treasury bulletins:\n- treasury_bulletin_2012_06 - June 2012 (which would contain data for FY2012 or early FY2013)\n- treasury_bulletin_2022_06 - June 2022 (which would contain data for FY2022 or early FY2023)\n\nBut I need to understand what \"FY2013 budget proposal release month\" and \"FY2023 budget proposal release month\" mean. Budget proposals are typically released in February of the prior fiscal year. So:\n- FY2013 budget proposal would be released in February 2012\n- FY2023 budget proposal would be released in February 2022\n\nLet me check the pages more carefully. The data shows \"Second-Quarter Net Budget Receipts by Source\" for:\n- FY2012: January, February, March\n- FY2022: January, February, March\n\nBut wait - the question is asking about FY2013 and FY2023 budget proposal release months. When are budget proposals released?\n\nThe President's budget proposal for a fiscal year is typically submitted to Congress in February of the preceding calendar year. So:\n- FY2013 budget proposal = February 2012\n- FY2023 budget proposal = February 2022\n\nNow I need to find the Employment and General Retirement net budget receipts for February 2012 and February 2022.\n\nLooking at the data:\n- In the 2012 bulletin (page 18), for FY2012 second quarter (Jan-Mar): Employment and general retirement: Jan = 74.8, Feb = 60.6, Mar = 69.3 (billions)\n\n\n- In the 2022 bulletin (page 20), for FY2022 second quarter (Jan-Mar): Employment and general retirement: Jan = 129.7, Feb = 104.6, Mar = 115.4 (billions)\n\nI'll calculate the percentage increase in Employment and General Retirement net budget receipts between February 2012 and February 2022. The receipts grew from $60.6 billion to $104.6 billion, representing a significant rise. I'll determine the exact percentage growth using the standard formula for percentage increase.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_89e509ab6bc39473","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# Employment and general retirement net budget receipts (in billions)\nfeb_2012 = 60.6\nfeb_2022 = 104.6\n\n# Calculate percentage growth\ngrowth = ((feb_2022 - feb_2012) / feb_2012) * 100\n\nprint(f'February 2012: ${feb_2012} billion')\nprint(f'February 2022: ${feb_2022} billion')\nprint(f'Growth: {((feb_2022 - feb_2012) / feb_2012) * 100:.2f}%')\nprint(f'Rounded to nearest whole number: {round(growth)}%')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
